Data sources (web parity; web hook names kept at Swift call sites):
  useChargingSessionsPaginated -> CostAnalysisDataSource.loadChargingSessionsPaginated(vehicleID,start,end)
  useCostForecast -> GET /analytics/cost-forecast [vehicle_id, months] -> loadCostForecast(vehicleID,months)
  bound through CostAnalysisPageModel (no networking in the view, ADR-004); the whole
  rollup is the single derived `analytics` bundle (web `useCostAnalysisData`).
SI discipline (ADR-005): session energy stays SI watt-hours, power SI watts, odometers SI
  meters. Energies surface as kWh (the web forces `convertEnergyFromSI(wh,'kWh')`); distance
  converts to the user unit ONLY at the render boundary via the shared Units facade
  (Units.convertDistance) in CostAnalysisFormat. Money uses the user currency symbol.
Full-page reproduction (no scope narrowing): all web sections rebuilt natively — 6 summary
  cards, monthly-cost + cost/kWh charts, charger-type donut+bars, gas-vs-EV calculator,
  monthly table, time-of-use bars+insights, AI-narration slot (injectable, baseline empty),
  cost-forecast chart + breakdown/savings/insights details + cost/kWh trend, and the
  lifetime-summary + environmental-impact pair. Every section renders its own empty state.

