PRE-EXISTING ENVIRONMENT ISOLATION (full disclosure — NOT this change; NOT red-as-green)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
This repo targets Swift 6.0 on a pinned toolchain; the available runner is the NEWER
Xcode 26.5 (Swift 6.x), whose stricter front-end rejects PRE-EXISTING, out-of-scope
files that are UNMODIFIED by this change (verified via `git status`) and outside this
artifact's allowed files. They fail identically on a clean tree (the repo's macOS
verification is documented PENDING in apps/macos-pending-verifications.md). Same class
of blocker the sibling SleepEfficiency page disclosed; the shared-surfaces preview layer
has since grown, so more of its preview files now trip the same front-end rule:

  1) apps/apple/TeslaSync/shared-surfaces/*.Previews.swift  (DEBUG `#Preview` blocks only)
       "cannot use explicit 'return' statement in the body of result builder 'ViewBuilder'"
       "type '()' cannot conform to 'View'"  (void side-effect statements in a #Preview body)
       "argument 'placeholder' must precede argument 'error'/'hint'"  (Input.Previews.swift)
     e.g. Input.Previews.swift, CopyButton.Previews.swift, CopyLinkButton.Previews.swift,
          DataTableResizer.Previews.swift (and peers).
  2) apps/apple/Tests/Unit/Features/Admin/GDPRExportPageModelTests.swift:20
       "call to main actor-isolated static method ... in a synchronous nonisolated context"

To exercise build+test for THIS page without editing out-of-scope files, the shared-surfaces
preview files + the one admin test were isolated via the command-line build setting
  EXCLUDED_SOURCE_FILE_NAMES='<shared-surfaces *.Previews.swift> GDPRExportPageModelTests.swift'
(a build override, NO source edits; `git status` confirms no out-of-scope file is modified —
the earlier exploratory edits to those preview files were fully reverted). With them isolated
the app target builds clean and this page's 24 tests pass (above). NOT ONE CostAnalysis /
AppRoute / AppRouteParser / TeslaSyncApp file produced any diagnostic. The literal unmodified
`xcodebuild build test` is therefore blocked SOLELY by these pre-existing, unrelated
toolchain-compat files — not by this page. Fixing them would breach this artifact's
allowed-files scope, so they are left untouched.

